US Treasury Macro Factors — Chapter 5.1 Research Framework
Part 1 — Historical Treasury Performance
Index Selection and Return Convention
The primary Bloomberg instrument for broad US Treasury total returns is LUATTRUU Index (Bloomberg US Treasury Total Return Unhedged USD). This is a market-value-weighted index of US Treasury securities and reinvests coupon income. It is a total-return index, not a price-return index.
Important caveat on historical coverage: The chapter reports performance beginning in 1973. The Bloomberg US Aggregate family (including LUATTRUU) was formally launched in 1986, with back-history extended to January 1973 using reconstructed data. The 1973–1986 segment is a backfill, not live index history. The chapter's drawdown figures (1977–1981: −25.5%; 2020–2023: −23.1%) are consistent with this reconstructed history. Users should treat the pre-1986 segment as a modeled approximation, not a live investable index.
