Drawdown Calculation Convention
A drawdown is calculated from the cumulative total-return index level as:
Drawdown(t) = Index(t) / max(Index(s), s ≤ t) − 1

This uses the gross total-return index level, not yield changes. Do not approximate drawdowns using duration × yield change; that approximation omits convexity and coupon reinvestment effects and is not appropriate for multi-year drawdown measurement.
To reproduce the chapter's drawdowns, download LUATTRUU Index with field TOT_RETURN_INDEX_GROSS_DVDS from 1973-01-01 and compute rolling peak-to-trough declines. The BDH formula is:
=BDH("LUATTRUU Index","TOT_RETURN_INDEX_GROSS_DVDS","1973-01-01","","Per=M")

