Factor 6 — Inflation-Conditioned Diversification Regime
This factor investigates whether the level or momentum of inflation compensation predicts subsequent stock–bond correlation. Candidate predictors:

USGGBE10 Index level (10Y breakeven)
BE_MOM_60D (Factor 1)
REAL_YIELD_MOM_60D (Factor 3)
CPI YoY trend (using eco_release_dt for publication-aware alignment)

The evaluation requires regressing STOCK_BOND_CORR_60D(t+h) on each predictor at time t, using only information available at t. Given that SPXT begins in 1989 and TIPS/breakeven data begins post-1997, the usable sample for this factor is approximately 1997–present (~27 years of daily data).
